@astervolans/dsh-literature-search README · @astervolans/dsh-literature-search：A DeepSeek Harness (dsh) plugin that searches the literature through the
**official PubMed NCBI E-utilities API** and **Google Scholar**, and returns
both backends as one shared `paper` shape.

@astervolans/dsh-literature-search README · @astervolans/dsh-literature-search：> The API research behind these choices — parameters, rate limits, response
> shapes, measured evidence and rejected alternatives — is written up in
> [`docs/API-RESEARCH.md`](docs/API-RESEARCH.md) (Chinese).

@astervolans/dsh-literature-search README · From a source checkout (offline)：```powershell
powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File install.ps1 -Profile desktop
```

@astervolans/dsh-literature-search README · Configuration page：The client plugin (`lib/client.js`) registers this bundle's configuration into
the **Plugins panel**, on the row `cordis.patch.yml` declares, and the server
side exposes `/plugin/literature-search` to back it:

@astervolans/dsh-literature-search README · Where the page lives：`@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-ui-plugin-manager` owns the sidebar's 插件 / Plugins
panel and declares one slot per plugin-configuration cell. This bundle uses
`plugins.bundle.config`, a **keyed** slot whose key is the **bundle's package
name** — the page belongs to the package, not to one of its rows:

```js
ctx.slots.inject('plugins.bundle.config', () =>
  ctx.slots.register({ name: 'plugins.bundle.config', key: CONFIG_KEY }, LiteratureSearchConfig)
);
```

@astervolans/dsh-literature-search README · The three sections：PubMed, Google Scholar and 通用 are three collapsible sections built by
`ConfigSection`: a `<button>` header (so the disclosure is keyboard-reachable and
the whole strip is the hit target) plus a body that is absent while collapsed.

@astervolans/dsh-literature-search README · How the page is provided (DSH 2.x)：Implementation notes: `lib/web.js` owns the routes and fact collection;
`lib/client.js` is a hand-written module-loader bundle
(`window.__ModuleLoader__.load`, with `require("react")` resolved by the DSH
client runtime). **There is no build step.**

@astervolans/dsh-literature-search README · How keys are stored, and how their state is decided：Each key slot is judged by **independent probes**, and a non-sensitive
diagnostic line (`ref=` / `describe=` / `resolve=` / `settings-secret=` /
`error=`) is printed under the badge:

@astervolans/dsh-literature-search README · How keys are stored, and how their state is decided：1. **The credential service** (`ctx.credentials`, writing
   `$DSH_HOME/.credentials.yaml`) — preferred;
2. **The in-settings key fields** (`pubmedApiKey` / `scholarSerpApiKey`,
   marked `role('secret')` and redacted on read) — used automatically when the
   current composition has **no** credential service. `resolveSecret` prefers
   it too.

